# UpRank Dashboard Rules

## Business clock

- Never use `Date.now()` for metric windows.
- Pass an explicit `referenceDate` into metrics (default/fallback 2026-11-01; prefer `X-Mock-Reference-Date` from sync).
- Use dayjs UTC helpers in `@/lib/reference-date` for diffs/month keys.

## Money & dates

- Billing amounts are **cents** (AUD). Convert to dollars only at display boundaries.
- Product `ads.monthly_budget` is whole AUD paid to the ad platform, not our revenue.
- Billing dates are Unix seconds; product dates are ISO 8601.

## Auth headers

- Billing: `Authorization: Bearer ${MOCK_API_KEY}`
- Product: `X-API-Key: ${MOCK_API_KEY}`

## Data join

- Join product `Client.stripeCustomerId` to billing `Customer.id`.

## Architecture

- Sync live mock APIs into Postgres; dashboard reads DB via SSR (`load-dashboard`), not a separate dashboard JSON API.
- Metrics are pure functions under `src/lib/metrics/` — unit-test **formulas/thresholds** only (health, retention, ads, LTV, cancel counts). Do not add tests that only assert SEO/label string maps.
- Keep the `shadcn` npm package: `src/app/globals.css` imports `shadcn/tailwind.css` (not just a CLI).
- API routes validate with Zod; no `any`.
- Imports stay at file top.
- Exhaustive `switch` on unions with a `never` default.
- Clone/setup instructions live in `README.md` — keep them accurate when sync UX or scripts change.
- Style: Prettier (`.prettierrc.json`) + ESLint (`eslint-config-next` + `eslint-config-prettier`). Pre-commit via husky → lint-staged. Use `pnpm check` before push.

## Ads add-on

- Detect via subscription item `productId === "prod_ads_management"` (or price id `price_ads_management`).
- Product `adsEnabled` is a secondary signal only.
